# RXScan privacy gate - reviewed exceptions.
#
# Format: <detector-id>|<path>|<value-sha256-prefix>|<reason>
#
# Exceptions are keyed on the VALUE DIGEST, never on the path alone. Clearing
# one known fixture therefore never blinds the detector to a different value
# appearing in that same file later. A digest of `*` is reserved for values
# that are structural (a forbidden-path needle list, say) rather than data,
# and should be avoided: it re-opens the whole file.
#
# Every entry below was reviewed by hand. The matched value is never recorded
# here - only its SHA-256 prefix - so this file is safe to commit.
#
# Adding an entry is a reviewed decision. Do not add one to make a gate green
# without recording why the value is safe to ship.
